= The Well

The energy levels are the set $Set(E_n; n in NN)$, also written $Set(E_1, E_2, dots;)$
or $Set((n, E_n); n >= 1, E_n < V_0)$. With $hbar$ the reduced Planck constant,
$ i hbar pdv(, t) ket(psi) = hat(H) ket(psi), quad
  braket(psi) = 1, quad braket(phi, psi) = integral phi^* psi dd(x), \
  mel(m, hat(x), n) = sqrt(hbar / (2 m omega)) (sqrt(n) delta_(m, n-1) + sqrt(n+1) delta_(m, n+1)). $ <eq-qm>
Projectors are $ketbra(n)$ and transitions $ketbra(m, n)$; a bra alone is $bra(phi)$, a
tall one $bra(vec(1, 0))$. Expectation values: $expval(hat(p))$, $expval(hat(x)^2, psi)$,
$ expval(hat(H)) = evaluated(pdv(, beta) (-ln Z))_(beta = 1 slash k T) + Order(hbar^2),
  quad f(x) = order(x^2) quad (x -> 0). $ <eq-exp>
As @eq-qm shows, the matrix of $hat(x)$ is tridiagonal; its trace and rank are
$tr hat(x) = 0$ and $rank hat(x) = oo$, and $Re z$, $Im z$, $sgn x$, $Res_(z = 0) f$,
$diag(1, 2)$, $trace A$, $Trace A$ are available as operators.

Near the minimum $x_0$ the potential is expanded term by term:
$ U(x) approx taylorterm(U, x, x_0, 0) + taylorterm(U, x, x_0, 1) + taylorterm(U, x, x_0, 2) \
  + dots + taylorterm(U, x, x_0, n) + taylorterm(U, x, a + b, k - 1). $ <eq-taylor>

= Relativity and Nuclei

Index positions are kept apart: $tensor(T, +mu, -nu)$, $tensor(Gamma, +lambda, -mu, -nu)$,
$tensor(R, -a, -b, +c, -d)$, $tensor(epsilon, -i, -j, -k)$, with
$ tensor(R, +rho, -sigma, -mu, -nu) = partial_mu tensor(Gamma, +rho, -nu, -sigma)
  - partial_nu tensor(Gamma, +rho, -mu, -sigma)
  + tensor(Gamma, +rho, -mu, -lambda) tensor(Gamma, +lambda, -nu, -sigma)
  - tensor(Gamma, +rho, -nu, -lambda) tensor(Gamma, +lambda, -mu, -sigma). $ <eq-riemann>
A decay chain: $isotope(U, a: 238, z: 92) -> isotope("Th", a: 234, z: 90) + isotope("He", a: 4, z: 2)$,
then $isotope("Th", a: 234) -> isotope("Pa", a: 234) + e^- + macron(nu)_e$, and the neutral
$isotope(n, a: 1, z: 0)$.

